<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-6">
  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Config",
    subtitle: "Tune global addon settings and model-level publishable behavior (routing, schedule, and SEO capabilities).",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-8">
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "RecordingStudioPublishable::Configuration",
        subtitle: "Set global defaults in the initializer and prefer model-level publishable declarations for per-type routing."
      ) %>

      <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
        language: :ruby,
        code: <<~RUBY
          RecordingStudioPublishable.configure do |config|
            config.default_time_zone = "America/Los_Angeles"
            config.layout = "recording_studio_publishable/application"
            config.canonical_redirect_status = :found
          end

          class Page < ApplicationRecord
            include RecordingStudioPublishable::ParentRecordable

            recording_studio_publishable(
              public_controller: "pages",
              public_action: :show,
              schedule: false,
              seo: false
            )
          end

          class Article < ApplicationRecord
            include RecordingStudioPublishable::ParentRecordable

            recording_studio_publishable(
              public_controller: "articles",
              public_action: :show,
              path: "/blogs/:uuid/:slug",
              schedule: true,
              seo: true
            )
          end
        RUBY
      ) %>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Available settings",
        subtitle: "These are the primary configuration points exposed by the addon."
      ) %>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-7 text-(--surface-muted-content-color)">
        <p><strong>management_authorizer</strong> (optional override) decides whether a user may edit publishable content. Receives <code>recording:</code> and <code>actor:</code> keyword args. By default, the gem uses <code>RecordingStudioAccessible.authorized?(role: :edit)</code> when available.</p>
        <p><strong>layout</strong> (optional) sets the layout for all gem-managed screens (default: <code>"application"</code>).</p>
        <p><strong>default_time_zone</strong> (optional) sets the fallback time zone used for publish/unpublish scheduling.</p>
        <p><strong>canonical_redirect_status</strong> (optional) sets the status code for stale slug redirects (default: <code>:moved_permanently</code>).</p>
        <p><strong>recording_studio_publishable</strong> (model DSL) is the recommended place to define per-model public controller/action/path and capability flags like <code>schedule:</code> and <code>seo:</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Model-level setup (recommended)",
        subtitle: "Define route mapping and feature capabilities close to each recordable model."
      ) %>

      <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
        language: :ruby,
        code: <<~RUBY
          class Page < ApplicationRecord
            include RecordingStudioPublishable::ParentRecordable

            recording_studio_publishable(
              public_controller: "pages",
              public_action: :show,
              schedule: false,
              seo: false
            )
          end

          class Article < ApplicationRecord
            include RecordingStudioPublishable::ParentRecordable

            recording_studio_publishable(
              public_controller: "articles",
              public_action: :show,
              path: "/blogs/:uuid/:slug",
              schedule: true,
              seo: true
            )
          end
        RUBY
      ) %>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-7 text-(--surface-muted-content-color)">
        <p>Set <code>schedule: false</code> to hide schedule controls and ignore scheduling parameters for that model.</p>
        <p>Set <code>seo: false</code> to disable SEO-only tags (<code>title</code>, <code>meta[name=description]</code>, <code>canonical</code>) while still allowing social tags.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Initializer example (global settings)",
        subtitle: "Use the initializer for cross-cutting defaults and authorization policy."
      ) %>

      <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
        language: :ruby,
        code: <<~RUBY
          RecordingStudioPublishable.configure do |config|
            config.default_time_zone = "America/Los_Angeles"
            config.layout = "recording_studio_publishable/application"
            config.canonical_redirect_status = :found

            config.management_authorizer = lambda do |recording:, actor:, **|
              actor.present? &&
                recording.present? &&
                defined?(RecordingStudioAccessible) &&
                RecordingStudioAccessible.authorized?(actor: actor, recording: recording, role: :edit)
            end
          end
        RUBY
      ) %>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Public head helper",
        subtitle: "Add the helper to the host app layout head so published pages emit SEO and social tags automatically."
      ) %>

      <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
        language: :erb,
        code: [
          "<!-- app/views/layouts/application.html.erb -->",
          "<head>",
          "  <" + "%= publishable_head_tags " + "%" + ">",
          "</head>"
        ].join("\n")
      ) %>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-7 text-(--surface-muted-content-color)">
        <p>Call the helper from the layout that renders your published pages. It uses the current <code>@publishable</code> and <code>@publishable_recording</code> instance variables when they are present.</p>
        <p>You can also pass explicit arguments if your host app wants to supply a custom public URL, title, description, or social image URL.</p>
        <p>The helper emits tags only when the publishable is currently live. If a record is still scheduled, no head tags are emitted yet.</p>
        <p>When <code>seo: false</code> on a model, SEO tags are skipped but social Open Graph/Twitter tags still render for live records.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Related guidance",
        subtitle: "These settings work together with the install generator and the public route helpers."
      ) %>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-7 text-(--surface-muted-content-color)">
        <p>Use model-level <code>recording_studio_publishable</code> declarations for per-type public routing and feature flags.</p>
        <p>Keep the initializer focused on cross-cutting behavior like authorization, layout, default time zone, and redirect status.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
